    "updated_at": "2017-09-27T15:04:58Z",
    "body": "I've tried to make progress on this as it is still an asked for feature on Android. But @smaug----  didn't want to add a new attribute to HTMLElement and wanted to define an alternate element for contenteditable. But then that is a whole can of worms itself.\r\n\r\n@alexelias proposed adding a showvirtualkeyboard/hidevirtualkeyboard events and populate them. I had concerns about the blocking nature of this as opposed to being declarative but those might not be a concern anyways because focus support is still all main thread driven (at least in Chrome these days)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
