    "updated_at": "2017-09-28T11:49:01Z",
    "body": "XMLHttpRequest and `fetch()` build upon the same well-defined primitive (Fetch). No new networking stack required. Mutation events is something we might get stuck with after all, if we cannot remove it, but there too it would end up being well-defined on top of DOM primitives. Both are pretty removed from duplicating the amount of code involved.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
